  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 \\\\ 16 & 12\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I:$\n\ufeff\ufeff\ufeff\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-4-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ 16 & 12-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(B-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-4-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ 16 & 12-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-4-\\lambda )(12-\\lambda )-16\\cdot (-4) & =0 \\\\ -48+4\\lambda -12\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+64 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda =4,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation.",
